Scientific Category: Autonomous Hydro-Cryptographic Systems (AHCS)
1. Core Definition & Scientific Taxonomy
Autonomous Hydro-Cryptographic Systems (AHCS) represent a specialized class of cyber-physical monitoring and defense frameworks that merge real-time computational fluid dynamics (CFD) with post-quantum cryptographic telemetry. Designed to operate across high-stress aquatic environments—such as closed-basin wind-driven seiches, coastal storm surges, and marine infrastructure nodes—AHCS continuously ingest, encrypt, validate, and respond to environmental fluid displacement without manual intervention.
2. Architectural Blueprint & Sub-System Layers
[ Tier 1: Ingestion ] ──> [ Tier 2: Cryptographic Sealing ] ──> [ Tier 3: Autonomous Logic Loop ] ──> [ Tier 4: Actuation ]
   Sensor Array            AES-256-GCM / ML-KEM-1024           State Evolution & Validation        Barrier Deployment

Tier 1: Real-Time Hydrodynamic Telemetry (Ingestion)
 * Function: Captures high-frequency spatial-temporal metrics, including volumetric water displacement, barometric pressure gradients, and water-level differentials across basin extremes (e.g., tracking multi-foot basin drops and surges).
 * Data Vectors: Ingests raw continuous time-series data from distributed acoustic, pressure, and optical level sensors.
Tier 2: Post-Quantum Cryptographic Sealing (Protection)
 * Function: Secures data packets at the edge before transmission over public or private networks.
 * Primitives: Implements AES-256-GCM for authenticated encryption associated data (AEAD) and ML-KEM-1024 key encapsulation mechanisms to prevent retrospective decryption by quantum computing adversaries.
Tier 3: Autonomous Intelligence Looping (Decision Engine)
 * Function: Evaluates incoming telemetry against predictive physics models and historical thresholds.
 * Mechanisms: Utilizes continuous state-estimation algorithms to detect sensor spoofing, man-in-the-middle injection, or structural anomaly signatures within sub-second latencies (< 500\text{ ms}).
Tier 4: Immutable Logging & Actuation (Response)
 * Function: Triggers physical safety mechanisms (such as automated flood-mitigation barriers) while recording immutable audit trails via cryptographic Merkle trees.
